        "reachable": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1999-dii:R0005",
      "text": "In a degraded communications environment, there is a need, for example, to be able to reset session time-out values if the data management services are being accessed by users affected by the communications degradation. At a minimum, the session time-out values shall be user definable and be able to be reset prior to initialization of a user session. The goal is to provide the option of dynamically changing session time values based on current communications performance identified by capabilities of the network management or DBMS.",
      "class": "FR",
      "subtype": null,
      "subtype_name": null,
      "promise_subtype": null,
      "tier": "primary",
      "label_source": "section",
      "confidence": 0.85,
